body:
Please let me know if you plan to add the cuda kernel example to some unit test in the repo.


Since evaluation is performed by the test.py file generated from the template, I updated the template to include code that JIT-compiles CUDA kernels via load_inline. The compiled function is then loaded and made available for further use.

If you'd like to test CUDA kernel loading, here are two example files for a simple CUDA kernel that performs element-wise addition:

kernel.cu
```C++
#include <torch/extension.h>
#include <ATen/cuda/CUDAContext.h>
template <typename scalar_t>
__global__ void add__Tensor_kernel(
    const scalar_t* __restrict__ x,
    const scalar_t* __restrict__ y,
    scalar_t* __restrict__ output,
    const int size) {
    const auto index = blockIdx.x * blockDim.x + threadIdx.x;
    if (index < size) {
        output[index] = x[index] + y[index];
    }
}
at::Tensor kernel_function(const at::Tensor& a, const at::Tensor& b) {
    TORCH_CHECK(a.dtype() == b.dtype(), "Input dtypes must match");
    auto out = at::empty_like(a);
    const int64_t numel = a.numel();
    const int threads = 256;
    const int blocks = (numel + threads - 1) / threads;
    AT_DISPATCH_FLOATING_TYPES_AND2(at::kBFloat16, at::kHalf, a.scalar_type(), "add__Tensor_kernel", ([&] {
        add__Tensor_kernel<scalar_t><<<blocks, threads, 0, c10::cuda::getCurrentCUDAStream()>>>(
            a.data_ptr<scalar_t>(), b.data_ptr<scalar_t>(), out.data_ptr<scalar_t>(), numel);
    }));
    return out;
}
```

kernel.cpp
```C++
#include <torch/extension.h>
at::Tensor kernel_function(const at::Tensor& a, const at::Tensor& b);
```

When testing with the above CUDA kernel, you will observe the following results:
```
Performance Results:
  Triton kernel: 0.0104 ms
  PyTorch native: 0.0102 ms
  Speedup: 0.97x
PERF_METRICS:{"triton_ms": 0.01044310744051352, "pytorch_ms": 0.01016882359388047, "speedup": 0.9737354184857872}
PERFORMANCE FAILURE: Triton kernel is not faster than PyTorch.
```


Please let me know if you have any comments. If you plan to add the CUDA kernel example to a unit test in the repository, please let me know!

